From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: irisrun <irisrun@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:43:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 11/38] Add DragGesture and ScrollView, and scroll List

DragGesture becomes active once a touch moves its minimum distance and fails
if the touch lifts before that, so taps still reach views underneath. Its
value has the velocity of the last tenth of a second and predicted ends that
decelerate at UIScrollView's normal rate.

ScrollView is made of SwiftUI parts until upstream has one: the content is
laid out at its ideal size along the scrolling axes and moved by a
high-priority drag that only starts along those axes. It keeps moving after a
fling, stretches past its edges and springs back. Content outside the view is
clipped and hidden from touches, as a UIScrollView's bounds hide it. The
state lives in an observable reference, as gesture callbacks run several
times between updates and read @State as it was at the last one.

List rows now sit in a ScrollView, and the layer renderer clips to rectangles
and rounded rectangles.
